WEBVTT

00:07.466 --> 00:08.634
(HEART THUMPING)

00:16.267 --> 00:17.309
(THUMPING STOPS)

00:31.240 --> 00:33.576
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

00:39.039 --> 00:41.584
SAM: "You are a carcinogen,"

00:41.584 --> 00:43.085
I would say to her.

00:44.712 --> 00:46.338
"You are a tumor,

00:46.338 --> 00:48.299
"whose malignancy has defined

00:48.299 --> 00:51.218
"the ebb and flow
of all I've done,

00:51.218 --> 00:53.304
"of all I've tried to do.

00:53.304 --> 00:54.430
"And yet, in spite of that,

00:54.430 --> 00:56.557
"do you know how much space
you occupy

00:56.557 --> 00:58.559
"in the entirety of me?

00:59.435 --> 01:00.686
"This much.

01:01.687 --> 01:02.897
"You define my life,

01:02.897 --> 01:06.817
"and yet, this is how much
you matter to me.

01:06.817 --> 01:08.986
"If you hadn't shown up
on my door this morning,

01:08.986 --> 01:11.238
"I'd have gladly gone
the rest of my days

01:11.238 --> 01:12.698
"thinking of you regularly,

01:12.698 --> 01:14.366
"but from a distance,

01:14.366 --> 01:15.993
"flung from your orbit.

01:16.744 --> 01:17.912
"But now...

01:18.829 --> 01:20.915
"you are here

01:20.915 --> 01:25.377
"and the bile is rising
and taking the form of words.

01:25.377 --> 01:27.505
"And what these words mean is,

01:27.505 --> 01:28.756
"never have I known

01:28.756 --> 01:30.925
"how closely love
and hate are bound

01:30.925 --> 01:33.093
"than when I think of you
and realize

01:33.093 --> 01:34.762
"you deserve neither."

01:35.638 --> 01:37.723
(HEART BEATING)

01:49.652 --> 01:51.737
(ETHEREAL MUSIC PLAYING)

01:59.995 --> 02:04.375
♪ I'll kill you softly ♪

02:04.375 --> 02:08.170
♪ So sweetly, kindly ♪

02:09.004 --> 02:13.467
♪ I'm mesmerizing ♪

02:13.467 --> 02:17.096
♪ It's terrifying ♪

02:17.096 --> 02:20.432
-(HEART BEATING)
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

02:29.024 --> 02:30.734
♪ This black suit fits
like a glove ♪

02:30.734 --> 02:33.571
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

02:33.571 --> 02:35.322
♪ Won't lose myself
to a touch ♪

02:35.322 --> 02:36.949
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

02:38.033 --> 02:39.702
♪ This black suit fits
like a glove ♪

02:39.702 --> 02:42.454
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

02:42.454 --> 02:43.831
♪ My red heart freed
like a dove ♪

02:43.831 --> 02:45.541
♪ But you tell me
that it's never enough ♪

02:45.541 --> 02:46.667
♪ This is your burial ♪

02:46.667 --> 02:48.794
(BACKUP SINGER VOCALIZING)

02:54.800 --> 02:56.176
♪ This is your burial ♪

03:03.559 --> 03:04.935
♪ This is your burial ♪

03:04.935 --> 03:07.938
(VOCALIZING)

03:22.411 --> 03:23.495
(CONTINUES VOCALIZING)

03:35.716 --> 03:37.426
(VOCALIZING INTENSIFIES)

03:41.013 --> 03:42.556
♪ This black suit fits
like a glove ♪

03:42.556 --> 03:45.184
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

03:45.184 --> 03:46.977
♪ Won't lose myself
to a touch ♪

03:46.977 --> 03:49.855
♪ I was born to be
the widow of love ♪

03:49.855 --> 03:51.607
♪ This black suit
fits like a glove ♪

03:51.607 --> 03:53.233
♪ But your teeth
tell me I'm not enough ♪

03:53.233 --> 03:54.693
♪ This is your burial ♪

04:07.206 --> 04:10.417
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

04:10.417 --> 04:12.461
SAM: I hadn't seen her
in over 10 years.

04:12.461 --> 04:15.506
But I could tell she was
coming from a mile away.

04:17.091 --> 04:18.592
More than a mile.

04:19.218 --> 04:21.971
A thousand miles.

04:21.971 --> 04:24.807
I woke up that morning
with a taste in my mouth

04:24.807 --> 04:27.309
I hadn't felt in years.

04:28.519 --> 04:30.354
(WOMAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

04:32.272 --> 04:34.441
(WOMAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

04:34.441 --> 04:36.860
Is it... Is it a bit too rigid
here at the waist?

04:36.860 --> 04:38.362
WOMAN 2: How do you feel?
You feel okay?

04:39.196 --> 04:40.489
Yeah. I just... It's...

04:40.489 --> 04:42.658
-I do love how bold it is.
-Yeah.

04:43.617 --> 04:44.702
A whole new you.

04:46.537 --> 04:48.163
SAM: I cast it
out of my mind,

04:48.872 --> 04:50.457
but as the day went on,

04:51.375 --> 04:53.252
the taste left my mouth

04:53.252 --> 04:56.714
and traveled
to that space behind my eyes

04:56.714 --> 04:59.800
where it settled
and turned thick.

04:59.800 --> 05:02.594
By the time the late flights
from LAX to Heathrow

05:02.594 --> 05:04.054
were coming in
for their landing,

05:04.054 --> 05:07.933
I felt as if a secret twin
had grown in my skull.

05:14.023 --> 05:15.733
(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

05:21.155 --> 05:22.948
WOMAN 3: What's wrong?
Are you okay?

05:23.490 --> 05:24.533
(BREATH TREMBLING)

05:50.768 --> 05:51.852
(DISTANT SCREAMING)

05:55.439 --> 05:56.774
-(SCREAMING STOPS)
-(WHIMPERS)

05:58.901 --> 06:00.402
(SHRIEKS)

06:05.157 --> 06:06.408
SAM: It was calling,

06:07.576 --> 06:08.827
shouting,

06:11.872 --> 06:12.915
screaming,

06:15.626 --> 06:16.752
telling me

06:17.461 --> 06:18.754
it was coming.

06:20.214 --> 06:22.257
She was coming.

06:24.218 --> 06:25.511
She was here.

06:26.095 --> 06:27.971
(RAIN PATTERING)

06:57.626 --> 06:59.753
(MUFFLED DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

07:01.630 --> 07:03.507
(INDISTINCT CHATTER
IN BACKGROUND)

07:04.383 --> 07:06.260
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

07:12.224 --> 07:14.476
Uh, hi. Excuse me.
Hi. Can I help you?

07:14.476 --> 07:15.853
I'm looking for Sam.

07:15.853 --> 07:19.731
Oh, I'm afraid
Sam isn't available right now.

07:19.731 --> 07:20.941
Are you...

07:20.941 --> 07:22.109
Does Sam know you were coming?

07:22.109 --> 07:23.193
No, no.

07:23.193 --> 07:24.444
Okay, uh...

07:24.444 --> 07:27.114
Well, then could I just
ask you to just wait, uh...

07:28.157 --> 07:29.199
MARY: Sam?

07:29.700 --> 07:31.785
(PANTING) Sam?

07:31.785 --> 07:33.036
HILDA: Um...

07:33.036 --> 07:35.330
-Sam?
-Sorry, you really can't...

07:35.330 --> 07:37.374
-Uh...
-MARY: (PANTING) Sam?

07:37.374 --> 07:38.834
HILDA: Sam's not
seeing anybody

07:38.834 --> 07:40.043
-right now.
-Sam?

07:44.923 --> 07:46.175
Sam, I'm so sorry.

07:46.175 --> 07:48.594
I didn't see her coming,
she just came in. (PANTING)

07:51.054 --> 07:52.472
Sam, I need a dress.

07:53.265 --> 07:54.808
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

07:56.518 --> 07:58.604
SAM: Just landed?

07:58.604 --> 07:59.938
MARY: Yes.
SAM: From LA?

08:00.731 --> 08:02.357
Yes, I just came from...

08:02.357 --> 08:03.817
Would you like
something to eat?

08:04.568 --> 08:07.321
-Uh... No, I...
-Hilda,

08:07.321 --> 08:10.657
do we... do we have anything
to eat here?

08:10.657 --> 08:12.701
Um, not really, no.

08:12.701 --> 08:14.494
Okay. (CHUCKLING)
Well, there you go.

08:16.371 --> 08:17.915
Does anyone know you're here?

08:19.625 --> 08:21.418
-No.
-SAM: I... I...

08:21.418 --> 08:24.004
I must say,
I wish you had called.

08:24.004 --> 08:26.089
You might have noticed
we're a little underwater

08:26.089 --> 08:27.966
-at the moment.
-Would you have answered?

08:27.966 --> 08:29.843
(CHUCKLING) No,
but somebody would have.

08:29.843 --> 08:32.846
And they could have told you
we're very busy.

08:32.846 --> 08:34.556
Sam has her show coming up.

08:35.265 --> 08:36.642
MARY: Oh.

08:37.267 --> 08:38.268
Sorry.

08:38.268 --> 08:41.063
For not calling
or for just showing up?

08:42.064 --> 08:43.649
In general.

08:43.649 --> 08:47.194
Wouldn't you rather get
more specific?

08:47.194 --> 08:50.405
I just never had the chance
to say it before,

08:50.405 --> 08:53.492
-so...
-So the onus is on me then,

08:53.492 --> 08:55.827
to list off your offenses
one by one

08:55.827 --> 08:56.870
and cross-check them

08:56.870 --> 09:00.207
against the totality
of your "I'm sorry"?

09:01.250 --> 09:02.709
Oh, well.

09:02.709 --> 09:05.712
That hardly seems worth it,
does it?

09:06.588 --> 09:08.090
Making me do all the work,

09:08.090 --> 09:10.342
-just like you always do.
-I can go

09:10.342 --> 09:11.385
if you want.

09:11.385 --> 09:14.554
If you want to go, go.

09:14.554 --> 09:16.056
If you want to stay, stay.

09:16.056 --> 09:18.225
If you want to apologize,
you go for it.

09:18.225 --> 09:19.726
But if you stay,

09:19.726 --> 09:20.978
please stop doing

09:20.978 --> 09:22.229
that hovering thing
you always do,

09:22.229 --> 09:24.064
because it makes me
very nervous.

09:25.357 --> 09:28.110
-Sorry.
-You already said that.

09:29.611 --> 09:31.321
-I mean it.
-Say it two more times,

09:31.321 --> 09:32.614
so I believe you.

09:34.783 --> 09:36.201
-(INHALES)
-But not yet.

09:37.494 --> 09:41.290
Catch me by surprise
with your sincerity.

09:42.666 --> 09:46.086
Now, why don't you start
with why you're here?

09:46.795 --> 09:48.005
I really do need a dress.

09:48.005 --> 09:50.549
What, you don't have
a whole coterie of stylists

09:50.549 --> 09:52.301
to take care of that for you?

09:52.301 --> 09:54.636
No, I do. But it's not...

09:57.014 --> 09:58.098
working out.

09:58.098 --> 10:00.309
And this performance,
when is it?

10:00.309 --> 10:01.685
The 31st.

10:02.602 --> 10:04.730
-That's on Sunday?
-Yes.

10:05.480 --> 10:07.566
And today is?

10:09.484 --> 10:10.569
Thursday.

10:12.029 --> 10:14.614
Well, that's impossible.

10:14.614 --> 10:16.491
What's wrong
with the dress you have?

10:16.491 --> 10:18.118
I'm assuming you have one.

10:18.118 --> 10:19.745
It's just all wrong.

10:20.370 --> 10:21.747
SAM: May I see it?

10:24.207 --> 10:26.501
-So that's it?
-MARY: Yes.

10:27.377 --> 10:28.754
SAM: It's not a dress at all.

10:29.421 --> 10:30.922
Who made it?

10:30.922 --> 10:32.299
Saracen & Pare.

10:34.760 --> 10:36.720
SAM: Hmm.

10:36.720 --> 10:39.473
Tell me three things
that are wrong with it.

10:40.474 --> 10:42.017
It doesn't feel like me.

10:43.226 --> 10:46.021
Okay. It doesn't
feel like you. That's one.

10:47.481 --> 10:48.523
That's it.

10:49.232 --> 10:50.484
That's it?

10:51.360 --> 10:53.528
-Yes.
-So you,

10:53.528 --> 10:57.407
who have been dressed
by everyone

10:57.407 --> 10:59.284
and worn everything,

10:59.284 --> 11:01.787
who once paraded down
a red... (CHUCKLING) ...carpet

11:01.787 --> 11:04.247
wearing nothing
but freshly poured honey,

11:04.247 --> 11:06.666
you have somehow found

11:06.666 --> 11:09.002
the one outfit
in all of creation

11:09.002 --> 11:11.630
that doesn't feel like you?

11:11.630 --> 11:12.547
Yes.

11:12.547 --> 11:15.133
And you've come
crawling back to me

11:15.133 --> 11:17.969
because you know
I can do better?

11:17.969 --> 11:20.222
-Yes.
-Because I, above all others,

11:20.222 --> 11:21.681
know you?

11:21.681 --> 11:23.225
Because I didn't know
where else to go.

11:23.934 --> 11:24.976
Truly?

11:26.019 --> 11:27.229
Yes.

11:33.860 --> 11:36.780
Will you let me do
whatever I like?

11:38.031 --> 11:39.491
Yes. But...

11:39.491 --> 11:41.284
Will you do exactly as I say?

11:41.827 --> 11:43.328
Yes, within...

11:43.328 --> 11:45.205
And will you wear what I make?

11:46.248 --> 11:47.457
Yes.

11:48.083 --> 11:49.501
And can you stop time?

11:51.837 --> 11:52.879
(SNAPS FINGERS)

11:53.922 --> 11:55.173
Just did.

11:55.173 --> 11:57.342
(CLOCK TICKING)

11:57.342 --> 11:59.928
SAM: This is really
going to take some doing,

11:59.928 --> 12:02.222
if we're gonna pull this off.

12:02.222 --> 12:04.474
MARY: Just tell me
what I can do.

12:04.474 --> 12:06.226
SAM: You can just
keep talking.

12:06.226 --> 12:07.352
That's how this works.

12:07.352 --> 12:10.313
You tell me something
like how you're feeling,

12:10.313 --> 12:13.859
and I'll take those feelings
and turn them into a dress.

12:13.859 --> 12:17.946
The transubstantiation
of feeling.

12:17.946 --> 12:19.364
That's what we're doing here.

12:21.992 --> 12:23.326
Here we are.

12:23.326 --> 12:25.287
Now, as you can see,

12:25.287 --> 12:27.914
I've entered
my Ms. Havisham period

12:27.914 --> 12:29.833
very much ahead of schedule.

12:29.833 --> 12:33.086
This is where I come to cry
my eyes out in the dark.

12:40.719 --> 12:41.845
Stand here, please.

12:50.520 --> 12:52.731
Now, uh...

12:52.731 --> 12:56.359
I haven't had a new idea
in ages.

12:56.359 --> 12:57.903
Not a good one, at least.

12:57.903 --> 12:59.488
So if we're to do this,

12:59.488 --> 13:02.282
I'm just gonna
have to fasten things to you

13:02.282 --> 13:05.285
-until inspiration strikes.
-(METAL CLANKING)

13:07.579 --> 13:08.663
SAM: There we go.

13:13.585 --> 13:16.129
HILDA: Uh, can I take
your sweater?

13:17.756 --> 13:18.757
Yes.

13:18.757 --> 13:19.883
-Thank you.
-Mmm-hmm.

13:21.134 --> 13:22.135
So...

13:23.512 --> 13:26.890
So tell me more
about this dress we're making.

13:26.890 --> 13:28.934
What do you see in your head?

13:30.560 --> 13:31.603
Just...

13:33.146 --> 13:34.272
me.

13:34.272 --> 13:35.315
Just you?

13:35.982 --> 13:37.067
MARY: But...

13:38.401 --> 13:40.111
But all of me.

13:40.111 --> 13:44.032
I was thinking more like,
"What color?"

13:44.032 --> 13:45.367
-Uh...
-Hold still.

13:48.662 --> 13:49.996
Whatever you like.

13:50.455 --> 13:51.623
But no red.

13:51.623 --> 13:53.083
Do you have to be able
to move?

13:54.042 --> 13:55.418
-Yes.
-Dance?

13:55.418 --> 13:58.171
-Yes.
-Any stunts or harnesses?

13:58.171 --> 13:59.214
No.

13:59.214 --> 14:00.298
Backup dancers?

14:00.298 --> 14:01.591
-Nine.
-I'm not making

14:01.591 --> 14:02.884
-anything for them.
-I know.

14:02.884 --> 14:03.969
There's simply
not enough time.

14:03.969 --> 14:05.762
I know. You don't have to.
Just me.

14:06.263 --> 14:07.305
HILDA: Arms up.

14:11.268 --> 14:12.644
What song are you singing?

14:15.105 --> 14:16.690
Spooky Action.

14:16.690 --> 14:18.275
Hmm. I don't remember
that one.

14:19.025 --> 14:21.069
-'Cause it's new.
-Oh.

14:21.069 --> 14:22.654
That explains it then.

14:22.654 --> 14:23.905
Did you write it?

14:24.698 --> 14:26.032
Yes.

14:28.535 --> 14:30.161
I'll play it for you
if you want.

14:30.161 --> 14:31.496
Yes, maybe later.

14:32.581 --> 14:34.541
(PEN SCRIBBLING)

14:34.541 --> 14:35.667
It's good.

14:35.667 --> 14:37.836
I am sure it is.

14:38.837 --> 14:40.046
It might be
the best song ever written

14:40.046 --> 14:42.007
-in the history of songs.
-SAM: Mmm.

14:42.007 --> 14:43.633
Lift your shirt up
for me, please.

14:55.353 --> 14:56.646
You've gotten so tiny.

14:57.397 --> 14:58.982
The tiniest intruder.

15:01.901 --> 15:03.486
You're exactly the same.

15:03.486 --> 15:04.654
Oh, no, I'm not.

15:05.405 --> 15:06.489
You'll see.

15:07.490 --> 15:09.576
You'll see how I've changed.

15:11.036 --> 15:13.121
What the years
have made of me.

15:16.916 --> 15:19.169
Okay. That's good for now.
Thank you, Hilda.

15:24.382 --> 15:25.508
(SCRAPING)

15:26.635 --> 15:28.386
-Hilda.
-Yes?

15:28.386 --> 15:31.056
Hilda, would you run back
to the main house

15:31.056 --> 15:34.017
-and grab a few things for me?
-Mmm-hmm.

15:35.435 --> 15:37.062
SAM: What does this matter?

15:38.229 --> 15:40.148
-You know what I need?
-Of course.

15:40.148 --> 15:41.900
SAM: Uh, what about you?
Can we get you anything?

15:41.900 --> 15:44.110
-I'm fine. Thank you.
-SAM: Okay. Good.

15:44.110 --> 15:45.654
HILDA: Okay.
I'll be right back.

15:56.122 --> 15:57.916
(DOOR OPENS)

15:59.751 --> 16:00.794
(DOOR CLOSES)

16:04.881 --> 16:06.174
She's not gonna tell anyone...

16:06.174 --> 16:08.051
No. Don't worry.

16:08.051 --> 16:09.844
There are no spies
in our midst.

16:09.844 --> 16:14.349
I just need her
to bring me some things.

16:14.349 --> 16:17.060
Some old bric-a-brac,
a few bolts of fabric,

16:17.060 --> 16:18.436
and a good pair of scissors

16:18.436 --> 16:20.730
in case one of us has
the sudden desire to...

16:20.730 --> 16:22.732
-(GRUNTING)
-(GASPS SOFTLY)

16:28.738 --> 16:30.573
-(SCISSORS CLATTER)
-Okay.

16:30.573 --> 16:32.283
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)

17:05.191 --> 17:06.526
How's your mum?

17:08.862 --> 17:10.029
MARY: She died.

17:12.198 --> 17:13.199
I'm sorry.

17:15.702 --> 17:17.871
How are you?

17:22.000 --> 17:23.126
Same.

17:23.126 --> 17:25.420
You've been laying low.

17:25.420 --> 17:28.923
Am I right that this will be
your first outing

17:28.923 --> 17:30.800
-since...
-Since?

17:30.800 --> 17:33.970
Since whatever happened
happened.

17:33.970 --> 17:35.764
What do you think happened?

17:35.764 --> 17:38.308
Well, I... I saw that video.

17:38.308 --> 17:40.268
(CHUCKLING)
Everyone saw that video.

17:41.311 --> 17:42.812
Is there more to it than that?

17:45.482 --> 17:46.524
Yes.

17:48.610 --> 17:51.488
And when it first happened,
people kept asking me,

17:51.488 --> 17:52.822
what do I know,

17:52.822 --> 17:55.492
had I heard anything,
"Did she trip, did she jump?"

17:58.495 --> 17:59.704
What'd you say?

17:59.704 --> 18:02.123
People... said
you had a breakdown.

18:02.123 --> 18:04.626
I said, "No. She probably
just needed a break."

18:04.626 --> 18:07.253
Yeah. That was part of it.

18:09.339 --> 18:10.924
What are the other parts?

18:13.635 --> 18:14.928
I don't want to tell you.

18:15.553 --> 18:17.180
-Why?
-(INHALES)

18:17.931 --> 18:19.599
Because you'd laugh.

18:19.599 --> 18:21.392
-No, I wouldn't.
-Yes, you would.

18:21.392 --> 18:23.102
-(SNICKERING)
-You're laughing right now.

18:23.102 --> 18:24.395
(LAUGHING) I'm just...

18:24.395 --> 18:26.272
I'm just picturing
the worst possible thing

18:26.272 --> 18:28.107
that could have made you do
what you did.

18:28.650 --> 18:30.068
(LAUGHING) I...

18:31.194 --> 18:33.488
-What is it?
-It's not worth mentioning,

18:33.488 --> 18:35.865
but it's very funny.

18:35.865 --> 18:37.867
Well, that's why
I'm not gonna tell you.

18:37.867 --> 18:39.035
Except you will.

18:39.035 --> 18:41.162
Because you never would have

18:41.162 --> 18:42.622
brought it up
in the first place

18:42.622 --> 18:44.207
if you didn't want to.

18:44.207 --> 18:46.417
No, you want to tell me.

18:46.417 --> 18:48.920
You want me to know so badly,
you can hardly stand it.

18:48.920 --> 18:51.506
But it's okay. I can wait.

18:56.886 --> 18:59.013
Mmm. Mmm.

19:03.768 --> 19:04.978
No.

19:08.273 --> 19:09.566
No.

19:13.361 --> 19:14.404
Mmm.

19:31.588 --> 19:32.672
(MARY WHIMPERS)

19:36.968 --> 19:39.387
(HEART THUMPING)

19:45.226 --> 19:46.477
No.

19:51.065 --> 19:53.192
Right. No red.

19:55.486 --> 19:57.030
No red.

19:57.030 --> 19:59.908
What about your hair,
what's going on there?

19:59.908 --> 20:01.159
We should...

20:01.159 --> 20:02.577
We should talk
about your halo.

20:02.577 --> 20:03.578
No halo.

20:04.704 --> 20:05.997
At all?

20:05.997 --> 20:08.750
I want to get back
to the basics.

20:08.750 --> 20:11.294
I mean, it doesn't get
much more basic than that.

20:11.294 --> 20:12.837
It's sort of your thing.

20:12.837 --> 20:14.464
It was never meant
to be my thing.

20:14.464 --> 20:15.798
It was your thing.

20:15.798 --> 20:18.384
That's... that's not
how I recall it.

20:18.384 --> 20:19.385
But whatever the case,

20:19.385 --> 20:20.720
you've done
pretty well with it.

20:20.720 --> 20:22.972
-We'll do well without it.
-Will anyone recognize you

20:22.972 --> 20:24.140
without it?

20:24.140 --> 20:26.684
I don't know if anyone
actually truly comprehends

20:26.684 --> 20:28.561
-the shape of your...
-They hurt.

20:34.442 --> 20:37.320
Well, that's because whoever's
making them for you now

20:37.320 --> 20:38.947
keeps trying to up the ante.

20:40.031 --> 20:41.908
They're not doing it right.

20:41.908 --> 20:42.992
I could make you a new one

20:42.992 --> 20:44.369
-in two seconds flat...
-No.

20:44.369 --> 20:46.496
-Right. But, don't you...
-I said...

20:46.496 --> 20:48.122
Yes, I know what you said.

20:48.122 --> 20:49.374
You don't want to wear one,

20:49.374 --> 20:51.918
but what if I want you
to wear one?

20:54.295 --> 20:55.546
(ETHEREAL MUSIC PLAYING)

20:55.546 --> 20:58.091
MARY: ♪ I can't believe
what I found ♪

20:59.926 --> 21:04.514
♪ I'm staring into the dark
so powerful... ♪

21:04.514 --> 21:07.141
♪ My knees are pressed
to the ground ♪

21:08.893 --> 21:11.729
♪ I'm holdin' on
for dear life ♪

21:11.729 --> 21:13.690
♪ It's mythical ♪

21:13.690 --> 21:15.900
♪ Are you there?
Are you mine? ♪

21:15.900 --> 21:17.986
♪ Do you feel holy? ♪

21:17.986 --> 21:20.321
♪ Are you real or divine? ♪

21:20.321 --> 21:22.490
♪ Do you feel holy? ♪

21:22.490 --> 21:24.784
♪ Are you there?
Are you mine? ♪

21:24.784 --> 21:26.119
♪ Do you know? ♪

21:26.119 --> 21:30.081
-♪ Your spirit is calling me ♪
-(INHALES, EXHALES)

21:30.081 --> 21:31.791
What are we doing here?

21:32.875 --> 21:35.128
Are we reinventing you?

21:36.796 --> 21:37.880
(MUSIC STOPS)

21:37.880 --> 21:38.923
No.

21:41.050 --> 21:42.468
No, I...

21:44.554 --> 21:45.555
Just...

21:48.933 --> 21:51.019
I... I want to be...

21:52.353 --> 21:56.024
-Revelatory.
-No. I just, like... I want...

21:57.400 --> 21:59.318
-Profundity.
-(SUCKS AIR THROUGH TEETH)

21:59.318 --> 22:01.154
Mmm, more, um...

22:03.823 --> 22:06.784
-Authenticity.
-No. It's like...

22:06.784 --> 22:08.286
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

22:12.081 --> 22:13.374
Clarity.

22:15.209 --> 22:16.669
-Yes.
-Clarity.

22:16.669 --> 22:19.881
-So, reducing?
-Yes.

22:19.881 --> 22:22.508
-Peeling away everything...
-Yes. Yes.

22:22.508 --> 22:24.635
-...that's accumulated.
-Yes.

22:24.635 --> 22:26.054
-Old skin.
-Yes.

22:26.054 --> 22:27.513
-Barnacles.
-Yes

22:27.513 --> 22:28.723
Dead hair.

22:28.723 --> 22:30.183
Yes.

22:30.183 --> 22:31.768
All the old yous.

22:32.477 --> 22:33.978
I want to be sharp.

22:33.978 --> 22:36.189
You want me
to make you into a knife?

22:36.189 --> 22:37.774
I want to have a point.

22:39.442 --> 22:40.610
Got it.

22:42.987 --> 22:44.322
MARY: If this were
the first performance

22:44.322 --> 22:46.699
I ever gave,
how would you dress me?

22:46.699 --> 22:49.243
I did dress you
for your first performance.

22:49.243 --> 22:50.953
MARY: If it were
my last performance?

22:50.953 --> 22:52.580
Is that what this is?

22:53.456 --> 22:54.916
-Maybe.
-'Cause I could make you

22:54.916 --> 22:56.834
a funeral gown,

22:56.834 --> 22:58.252
if that's what
you really wanted.

22:58.252 --> 22:59.378
I could build you a pyre

22:59.378 --> 23:01.089
the likes of which
the world has never seen

23:01.089 --> 23:03.341
if that's the way
you see things going.

23:07.178 --> 23:08.763
I sort of do.

23:11.057 --> 23:12.600
We are still speaking in...

23:13.559 --> 23:14.977
abstractions, aren't we?

23:15.812 --> 23:17.271
(MARY'S BREATH TREMBLING)

23:17.271 --> 23:18.314
I think so.

23:18.815 --> 23:20.399
Are you depressed?

23:20.399 --> 23:22.110
-No. No.
-Is this a cry for help?

23:22.110 --> 23:24.779
So you're not planning
on self-immolating

23:24.779 --> 23:26.280
-on my doorstep?
-(INHALES)

23:26.280 --> 23:27.532
-No.
-Good.

23:27.532 --> 23:29.659
But if I did, it would be
kind of a great way to go.

23:29.659 --> 23:31.828
No, not for me. I'd be the one
to have to clean you up.

23:31.828 --> 23:33.329
-No peeking.
-(SNIFFLES)

23:36.207 --> 23:37.542
If it's really that bad,

23:38.459 --> 23:39.502
just quit.

23:39.502 --> 23:41.087
MARY: I can't quit.

23:41.087 --> 23:42.588
SAM: Yeah, you can.

23:42.588 --> 23:44.173
People say
quitting is for cowards,

23:44.173 --> 23:45.758
but it's actually
one of the bravest things

23:45.758 --> 23:48.511
-anyone can do.
-No. (BREATH TREMBLING)

23:48.511 --> 23:51.472
I can't quit. I don't know
how to do anything else.

23:53.182 --> 23:54.642
(SIGHS)

23:56.894 --> 23:58.354
I just wish
I was happy doing it.

23:58.354 --> 24:00.356
SAM: Oh, yes, I remember.

24:00.356 --> 24:05.319
Used to be so happy
singing sad songs. Well...

24:05.319 --> 24:08.489
things are never gonna
be like that ever again.

24:09.407 --> 24:12.243
Nevertheless...
you will go on.

24:12.243 --> 24:13.953
This won't be
your last performance ever

24:13.953 --> 24:15.746
but it will be your best.

24:15.746 --> 24:17.540
You will be radiant,

24:17.540 --> 24:19.375
and transcendent.

24:19.375 --> 24:22.420
And when you open your mouth
and sing about your sadness,

24:22.420 --> 24:23.963
it will be everyone's sadness,

24:23.963 --> 24:27.008
and it will be writ
as large as the goddamn sky

24:27.008 --> 24:29.677
because that's
what you give people.

24:30.636 --> 24:32.471
It's what
you can do for people

24:32.471 --> 24:34.724
and since they pay you for it,

24:34.724 --> 24:36.726
it's more or less your job,
so quit...

24:37.393 --> 24:38.686
or do a good job.

24:45.151 --> 24:46.152
See?

24:47.862 --> 24:49.530
This is what you do.

24:50.990 --> 24:53.576
This is why you have
nothing to worry about.

24:54.952 --> 24:58.247
You give people the gift
of giving a shit about you.

24:59.415 --> 25:03.294
I am humbled
by your munificence.

25:07.590 --> 25:08.591
Uh...

25:09.342 --> 25:11.344
Is someone playing before you?

25:12.637 --> 25:14.138
Yes.

25:14.138 --> 25:15.473
-Who?
-(INHALES)

25:15.473 --> 25:17.350
(SIGHS) Miel Contrera.

25:17.350 --> 25:18.768
What's she sing?

25:18.768 --> 25:21.479
-Paper Moon.
-Oh, right. Yeah, I like her.

25:22.396 --> 25:24.273
MARY: Everyone likes her.

25:24.273 --> 25:25.650
SAM: You sound bitter.

25:27.818 --> 25:28.945
No, I don't.

25:29.946 --> 25:31.322
She's my friend.

25:31.322 --> 25:32.990
-Is she?
-Yes.

25:32.990 --> 25:34.158
-We sang together at the...
-Yeah.

25:34.158 --> 25:36.327
But she was just a child then.

25:36.327 --> 25:37.578
Now I see her
everywhere I look.

25:37.578 --> 25:40.581
Her tits are spilling out
over Soho in Givenchy.

25:40.581 --> 25:42.166
She's successful

25:42.750 --> 25:43.918
and I'm proud of her.

25:43.918 --> 25:46.003
And I'm very happy
to be in her company.

25:46.003 --> 25:47.004
Good.

25:47.505 --> 25:49.257
But?

25:49.257 --> 25:52.677
You're going to lay waste
to her, aren't you?

25:52.677 --> 25:54.428
-What?
-Oh.

25:54.428 --> 25:56.889
Poor girl doesn't know
what she's in for.

25:56.889 --> 25:58.266
Why would you even say that?

25:58.266 --> 25:59.475
SAM: Because it's true.

25:59.475 --> 26:00.643
No, it's not.

26:00.643 --> 26:02.270
SAM: Oh,
it's already happened.

26:02.270 --> 26:04.438
You don't even have to try.

26:04.438 --> 26:05.856
This is what you do.
You're always picking

26:05.856 --> 26:08.025
-and picking and scratching...
-It's part of my job.

26:08.025 --> 26:09.860
I need to see
what I'm meant to cover.

26:09.860 --> 26:11.821
You mean you need to see
what you want to find.

26:11.821 --> 26:13.072
And if you don't find it,
you put it there

26:13.072 --> 26:14.699
because it suits you
and what you want to make,

26:14.699 --> 26:16.409
-which is why...
-Which is why I'm here

26:17.076 --> 26:18.577
-and you're there.
-No.

26:18.577 --> 26:20.079
I'm here because I want
what you want,

26:20.079 --> 26:22.248
but I want you to want it
for the right reasons.

26:22.248 --> 26:23.457
Which are?

26:23.457 --> 26:24.542
I want you
to have an open heart.

26:24.542 --> 26:26.627
-SAM: Mmm-hmm. Mmm.
-And no fear.

26:26.627 --> 26:28.587
And what am I afraid of?

26:28.587 --> 26:29.630
Of this.

26:30.089 --> 26:31.382
-Me.
-Yeah.

26:31.382 --> 26:32.842
Hey,
you're fucking terrifying.

26:34.802 --> 26:36.887
This is what you do.

26:36.887 --> 26:38.597
This is what you do when
you don't know what to do.

26:38.597 --> 26:39.849
This is what
you've always done,

26:39.849 --> 26:42.852
which is why I'm trying
to lay it all out for you.

26:42.852 --> 26:44.979
But I asked you
to lay it out for me

26:44.979 --> 26:47.106
so that I'd know what to do.

26:47.106 --> 26:49.358
-So, here it is.
-Thank you.

26:53.112 --> 26:55.323
Miel Contrera
will sing before me.

26:56.699 --> 27:00.286
She will sing Paper Moon,
and it'll be beautiful.

27:00.786 --> 27:02.163
And then,

27:02.163 --> 27:04.749
at five minutes to midnight,
the lights will go down.

27:06.917 --> 27:08.002
And I...

27:10.629 --> 27:11.756
SAM: Mmm-hmm.

27:12.590 --> 27:13.799
(EXHALES)

27:15.134 --> 27:17.970
I'll do whatever it is
that I'm gonna do.

27:20.723 --> 27:23.434
Sing your new song?

27:23.434 --> 27:24.435
Yes.

27:25.770 --> 27:27.480
Maybe not.

27:27.480 --> 27:30.232
-No, I'm gonna sing it.
-Oh, good.

27:30.232 --> 27:33.194
Because you sounded
uncertain there for a moment.

27:34.612 --> 27:36.655
No, it's just...

27:37.323 --> 27:38.574
It's not good enough yet?

27:43.496 --> 27:44.622
You want to hear it?

27:45.498 --> 27:46.874
The... the song?

27:46.874 --> 27:48.793
-Yes.
-No.

27:50.002 --> 27:51.796
No. No music.

27:52.797 --> 27:53.881
Not right now.

27:54.632 --> 27:56.926
-Why?
-Because if I did,

27:56.926 --> 27:58.219
I'd make a dress for the song.

27:58.219 --> 28:00.513
And you want me to make
a dress for you, don't you?

28:00.513 --> 28:03.140
So, better not to hear it.

28:04.058 --> 28:05.351
(SCISSORS SNIPPING)

28:05.351 --> 28:07.019
-You might like it.
-(SCISSORS CLATTER)

28:07.019 --> 28:09.480
Mmm, I'm in an ascetic phase
right now.

28:10.189 --> 28:12.149
I'm trying not liking things.

28:15.277 --> 28:17.696
Why is it called
Spooky Action anyway?

28:18.823 --> 28:21.826
Is it about particle physics?

28:21.826 --> 28:23.786
Large Hadron Colliders?

28:25.913 --> 28:28.874
MARY: No. It's more like...

28:29.875 --> 28:31.961
connections we can't explain.

28:31.961 --> 28:34.630
And what led you to write it?

28:37.591 --> 28:40.469
I had a connection
and I couldn't explain it.

28:41.053 --> 28:42.096
To a person?

28:43.097 --> 28:44.140
Maybe.

28:44.932 --> 28:46.016
Are you being coy?

28:46.642 --> 28:48.060
No.

28:48.060 --> 28:49.437
And you really can
dance to it?

28:51.230 --> 28:52.690
-Yes.
-Hmm.

28:54.733 --> 28:55.734
Show me.

28:57.319 --> 28:59.029
-The dance?
-Yeah.

28:59.864 --> 29:01.365
Could you?

29:01.365 --> 29:04.618
Honestly, it'll be good for me
to see how you move

29:04.618 --> 29:06.620
to make sure
I'm accommodating.

29:11.083 --> 29:12.293
Okay.

29:12.293 --> 29:14.462
I'm sure you're supposed to be
drilling it anyway.

29:18.883 --> 29:20.050
(CLEARS THROAT SOFTLY)

29:27.600 --> 29:28.642
(SHOE THUDS)

29:30.436 --> 29:31.479
(SHOE THUDS)

29:38.277 --> 29:40.738
Do you have a speaker
or anything I can plug into?

29:41.322 --> 29:42.907
Yeah.

29:42.907 --> 29:44.158
But do it without the song.

29:47.411 --> 29:48.829
Why?

29:48.829 --> 29:51.040
Because I told you,
I don't want to hear it.

29:51.040 --> 29:53.626
-But it's all set to the...
-I'm sure you've got it down.

29:55.503 --> 29:57.379
Why won't you just let me
play it for you?

29:57.379 --> 29:59.006
'Cause I don't want
to break my streak.

29:59.590 --> 30:00.716
Of what?

30:00.716 --> 30:02.218
Of not listening
to your music.

30:34.416 --> 30:35.543
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

30:39.004 --> 30:40.631
-(INHALES)
-(TAPS FLOOR)

30:40.631 --> 30:42.550
-(EXHALES)
-(TAPS FLOOR)

30:43.425 --> 30:44.885
-(EXHALES)
-(TAPS FLOOR)

31:07.324 --> 31:08.409
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

31:31.390 --> 31:32.808
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

31:44.403 --> 31:45.529
Ooh. Okay.

31:45.529 --> 31:47.114
-Well, I think that's...
-I'm not done yet.

32:01.337 --> 32:02.630
(TABLE THUDDING)

32:02.630 --> 32:03.631
(GRUNTS)

32:08.469 --> 32:09.845
(GRUNTS)

32:12.848 --> 32:14.099
(GRUNTS)

32:18.020 --> 32:19.730
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

32:20.314 --> 32:22.024
(BREATHING LOUDLY)

32:23.567 --> 32:25.611
(GRUNTING)

32:25.611 --> 32:27.071
(PANTING)

32:27.863 --> 32:28.906
(MARY GRUNTS)

32:36.455 --> 32:38.916
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

32:42.670 --> 32:44.338
(GRUNTS)

32:45.297 --> 32:47.091
(STRAINING)

32:48.967 --> 32:49.968
(GRUNTS)

32:58.185 --> 33:00.646
(PANTING)

33:19.832 --> 33:23.669
(SAM BREATHES DEEPLY)

33:26.130 --> 33:29.383
How on earth
are you gonna sing

33:29.383 --> 33:30.968
while you do all that?

33:31.593 --> 33:33.804
(PANTING)

33:33.804 --> 33:34.888
Practice.

33:37.141 --> 33:38.350
(EXHALES)

33:48.736 --> 33:50.028
(SAM TUTS)

33:50.028 --> 33:51.405
(MARY EXHALES)

33:51.405 --> 33:52.531
You know,

33:54.158 --> 33:55.868
if you're going for...

33:56.827 --> 34:01.123
burn-it-all-down
last-will-and-testaments,

34:01.915 --> 34:03.542
what we should do is

34:04.543 --> 34:06.128
we should make you
a beautiful dress

34:06.128 --> 34:07.463
that is simple and elegant,

34:07.463 --> 34:09.006
and whatever else
it needs to be,

34:09.006 --> 34:11.508
but attached to it...

34:12.968 --> 34:14.011
is a train.

34:14.011 --> 34:16.597
-(LAUGHING)
-You know how I love...

34:18.098 --> 34:20.851
a good train,
and this one is, say,

34:20.851 --> 34:23.312
um, just a quarter-mile long.

34:23.312 --> 34:26.231
And maybe
most people don't notice,

34:26.231 --> 34:29.276
but a keen eye will detect

34:29.276 --> 34:33.447
that at a certain point,
the fabric of the gown fades

34:33.989 --> 34:35.199
from one thing

34:35.824 --> 34:37.618
into something else.

34:37.618 --> 34:40.078
Something more familiar.

34:40.078 --> 34:42.122
It's so seamless
you don't even see it.

34:42.122 --> 34:43.791
But once you do,

34:44.875 --> 34:46.627
you realize

34:46.627 --> 34:51.006
the entire gown is made up
of every dress

34:51.006 --> 34:52.966
you've ever

34:52.966 --> 34:54.676
-worn.
-(EXHILARATING MUSIC PLAYING)

34:54.676 --> 34:57.346
The story
of how you got to right here,

34:57.763 --> 34:59.598
right now,

34:59.598 --> 35:02.184
in this exact moment,

35:02.184 --> 35:03.727
stepping out on stage,

35:03.727 --> 35:06.730
Mother Mary... (GASPS)
...in the new millennium.

35:06.730 --> 35:08.565
You walk...
(SUCKS AIR THROUGH TEETH)

35:08.565 --> 35:09.691
...down the...
Where is the show?

35:09.691 --> 35:13.153
-At the Palladium.
-That's perfect. So...

35:13.153 --> 35:15.864
Miel Contrera
finishes singing,

35:15.864 --> 35:18.784
and it's beautiful
and it's well-liked,

35:18.784 --> 35:22.162
but now, here you come,

35:22.996 --> 35:25.457
marching down that aisle,

35:25.457 --> 35:27.459
marching
from far beyond the aisle,

35:27.459 --> 35:29.169
from outside the theater,

35:29.169 --> 35:30.921
coming down the street,

35:30.921 --> 35:34.925
dragging your whole history
behind you.

35:35.509 --> 35:37.386
The doors swing open,

35:37.386 --> 35:38.554
and you enter the theater

35:38.554 --> 35:41.348
and you walk up
the steps to the stage,

35:41.348 --> 35:43.225
and when you get to the top...

35:43.976 --> 35:45.227
What's this?

35:46.436 --> 35:47.771
Something catches.

35:48.647 --> 35:51.233
The train is pulled tight.

35:51.233 --> 35:55.529
It's caught
on all of your history.

35:56.363 --> 35:59.116
And as you take
your final step

35:59.116 --> 36:01.410
and complete your ascension,

36:02.035 --> 36:04.037
the entire gown,

36:04.037 --> 36:07.499
we'll set it
so it just shears away,

36:07.499 --> 36:08.750
and there you are.

36:09.918 --> 36:15.549
You are standing naked
under the lights,

36:15.549 --> 36:18.218
free of everything
you've been carrying,

36:18.218 --> 36:21.054
of everything that's been
weighing you down.

36:21.054 --> 36:23.181
And, of course,
the plugs will get pulled

36:23.181 --> 36:26.226
and the broadcast would cut
but that's on them,

36:26.226 --> 36:27.728
it's not on you.

36:27.728 --> 36:29.146
Mmm-mmm.

36:29.146 --> 36:31.732
You're doing
what you were born to do.

36:32.608 --> 36:34.943
You open your mouth

36:34.943 --> 36:36.945
and you dance your dance.

36:38.572 --> 36:40.699
You sing your song.

36:41.950 --> 36:43.410
Or maybe...

36:44.620 --> 36:46.121
you don't even do that.

36:47.915 --> 36:49.791
Maybe you don't need to.

36:51.293 --> 36:54.755
You don't need
the song at all,

36:55.464 --> 36:56.965
because this...

36:58.508 --> 37:01.637
is all about...

37:02.971 --> 37:04.056
you.

37:12.564 --> 37:13.649
But...

37:19.488 --> 37:20.948
isn't that kind of...

37:27.746 --> 37:28.872
-obvious?
-No.

37:29.831 --> 37:33.001
Mmm. This is...

37:33.627 --> 37:34.711
clarity.

37:35.712 --> 37:38.840
♪ Bad conversations ♪

37:40.050 --> 37:42.719
♪ Cigarettes ♪

37:43.512 --> 37:46.056
♪ Words I don't mean ♪

37:47.307 --> 37:49.393
♪ Empty threats ♪

37:49.393 --> 37:51.436
♪ Chewing gum ♪

37:51.436 --> 37:54.773
♪ I'm so empty ♪

37:56.400 --> 38:00.112
♪ You're the one for me ♪

38:00.737 --> 38:02.698
♪ You see ♪

38:02.698 --> 38:05.534
♪ But it's been a while ♪

38:09.037 --> 38:13.208
♪ My mouth is lonely for you ♪

38:16.336 --> 38:20.632
♪ My mouth is lonely for you ♪

38:22.676 --> 38:24.553
♪ You ♪

38:26.596 --> 38:28.265
♪ My mouth ♪

38:31.226 --> 38:35.313
♪ My mouth is lonely for you ♪

38:35.313 --> 38:37.107
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

38:44.865 --> 38:46.783
(CHEERING DISTORTS, FADES)

38:47.868 --> 38:48.910
(GASPS)

38:50.412 --> 38:52.456
(PANTING)

39:34.498 --> 39:36.583
(ENCHANTING MUSIC PLAYING)

39:50.263 --> 39:53.141
♪ You said go find
all the things that you want ♪

39:53.141 --> 39:54.810
♪ Find all the things
that you need ♪

39:54.810 --> 39:58.271
♪ If you can't find them in me
go find anywhere, please ♪

39:58.271 --> 40:00.440
♪ Unroll the map
climb up the trees ♪

40:00.440 --> 40:02.359
♪ Scale the mountain
do or don't breathe ♪

40:02.359 --> 40:04.402
♪ But you must
fall to your knees ♪

40:04.402 --> 40:06.863
♪ Don't cry to the stars
you must summon the deep ♪

40:06.863 --> 40:08.490
♪ Lose all the people
you keep ♪

40:08.490 --> 40:09.616
♪ Lose your will to believe ♪

40:09.616 --> 40:10.826
♪ And once again believe ♪

40:10.826 --> 40:12.494
♪ And if in the end
you're not free ♪

40:12.494 --> 40:13.995
♪ Cut a deal, please ♪

40:13.995 --> 40:16.123
-(CLINKING)
-♪ Used to walk with you ♪

40:16.123 --> 40:19.709
♪ Till I saw
something bigger ♪

40:19.709 --> 40:21.795
♪ I jumped
into the flames ♪

40:21.795 --> 40:25.173
♪ And I shook hands
with forever ♪

40:25.173 --> 40:28.468
♪ Had to cut ties ♪

40:28.468 --> 40:29.886
(SNIFFING)

40:30.804 --> 40:33.598
♪ To be star-light ♪

40:36.810 --> 40:38.812
♪ He blessed me
with his gaze... ♪

40:38.812 --> 40:42.190
That was a very specific
moment in time,

40:42.774 --> 40:43.942
wasn't it?

40:44.860 --> 40:45.944
(HALO CLINKING)

40:45.944 --> 40:47.404
Why do we say that?

40:48.488 --> 40:50.532
Every moment in time
is specific.

40:50.532 --> 40:53.702
Yeah, but it's hard to tell
one from the next. Mmm?

40:54.619 --> 40:56.329
Every now and then, though,

40:57.330 --> 40:59.207
something happens.

41:00.375 --> 41:02.544
And it makes us
prick up our ears

41:02.544 --> 41:06.464
and say,
"That was a moment."

41:06.464 --> 41:09.426
And what I think
we're really saying...

41:09.426 --> 41:11.303
-(HALO CLINKING)
-...is for that moment,

41:12.888 --> 41:14.848
we were...

41:15.599 --> 41:16.641
together.

41:19.394 --> 41:21.563
Did you really mean
what you said?

41:22.355 --> 41:24.357
About what?

41:24.357 --> 41:26.776
About not listening
to my music.

41:30.155 --> 41:31.489
-Yes.
-(HALO CLATTERS)

41:32.616 --> 41:33.742
Is it a surprise?

41:33.742 --> 41:35.952
I don't exactly see you
at the runway.

41:35.952 --> 41:38.663
Did I really hurt
your feelings so badly?

41:38.663 --> 41:39.873
Yeah.

41:39.873 --> 41:41.708
And that's fine.

41:41.708 --> 41:43.710
That's what feelings are for.

41:43.710 --> 41:46.004
I just wish you would have
told me yourself.

41:47.172 --> 41:48.381
Told you what?

41:48.381 --> 41:50.258
(SMACKS LIPS) That, um...

41:51.259 --> 41:53.511
That Mother Mary no longer
needed me.

41:53.511 --> 41:55.639
-I did need you.
-No, you...

41:55.639 --> 41:57.390
-And I did tell you.
-You told me

41:57.390 --> 41:58.683
by not telling me.

41:58.683 --> 42:00.060
You told me by saying nothing

42:00.060 --> 42:02.604
and letting everyone
who suddenly had your ear

42:02.604 --> 42:03.647
do all the talking.

42:03.647 --> 42:04.940
I told you I needed a change.

42:04.940 --> 42:07.943
Yes, but you didn't tell me
you'd already made it.

42:07.943 --> 42:09.736
By the time
I figured that out,

42:09.736 --> 42:11.905
you'd already closed the door.

42:11.905 --> 42:13.198
The door was always open.

42:13.198 --> 42:14.282
No.

42:14.282 --> 42:15.367
No, it wasn't.

42:16.660 --> 42:18.662
No, it wasn't. It was shut

42:19.120 --> 42:20.664
and locked.

42:20.664 --> 42:22.874
And you were
a million miles away.

42:23.750 --> 42:25.335
And there I was...

42:25.335 --> 42:27.045
who knew you and...

42:29.839 --> 42:31.424
who loved you,

42:32.717 --> 42:36.096
trying to pick up the pieces.

42:36.096 --> 42:38.974
Except there weren't
even any pieces

42:38.974 --> 42:40.809
'cause everything I had was...

42:41.601 --> 42:43.853
wrapped up in you.

42:43.853 --> 42:46.314
You never know
how little you matter

42:46.314 --> 42:48.024
until you realize

42:48.024 --> 42:49.818
that everything you've done

42:49.818 --> 42:51.653
has been in the service

42:51.653 --> 42:54.114
of someone
the whole world loves

42:54.114 --> 42:56.366
just as much as you.

42:59.536 --> 43:03.498
Oh, yeah. And tell yourself
you're doing good work.

43:03.498 --> 43:05.083
Tell yourself
what you're doing counts

43:05.083 --> 43:06.543
'cause you're the one
that's doing it,

43:06.543 --> 43:09.587
but really, step by step,

43:09.587 --> 43:10.964
stitch by stitch,

43:12.882 --> 43:15.051
you're obliterating yourself.

43:20.015 --> 43:22.100
I wanted you

43:22.100 --> 43:23.810
to look like Joan of Arc.

43:27.230 --> 43:29.024
When I heard you sing,

43:29.941 --> 43:32.235
that's what I saw.

43:32.235 --> 43:36.573
That's what I set out
to design for you.

43:37.407 --> 43:38.700
And to that,

43:39.326 --> 43:42.120
I added bits and pieces

43:43.705 --> 43:44.706
of me.

43:46.750 --> 43:48.084
Silly things,

43:49.002 --> 43:52.339
like my holy communion
when I was seven.

43:52.339 --> 43:53.381
Feeling like a queen

43:53.381 --> 43:54.924
even though I'd spilled wine

43:54.924 --> 43:57.177
all down
my beautiful white dress.

44:00.221 --> 44:01.306
All of that

44:02.515 --> 44:03.725
is in there.

44:05.643 --> 44:07.228
That's my story.

44:08.855 --> 44:09.898
And no,

44:10.690 --> 44:12.275
I don't expect you to tell it.

44:13.526 --> 44:16.988
But I... would have expected
a little bit credit.

44:26.539 --> 44:29.209
-I didn't mean to cut you out.
-But you did.

44:30.502 --> 44:31.628
MARY: Yes.

44:32.379 --> 44:33.380
I did.

44:36.758 --> 44:38.635
-But...
-What?

44:38.635 --> 44:40.887
But I'm the one
who wore that dress,

44:42.597 --> 44:44.557
who wore all the dresses.

44:46.893 --> 44:47.977
I let you make

44:47.977 --> 44:50.355
-something of me.
-No. No.

44:50.355 --> 44:52.774
-We did that together.
-And...

44:52.774 --> 44:53.983
And I liked it.

44:54.943 --> 44:56.069
I liked it.

44:58.029 --> 44:59.739
I liked how you saw me.

45:03.451 --> 45:05.078
I liked how it felt...

45:07.288 --> 45:09.707
when you dressed me.

45:09.707 --> 45:13.086
But you were making
your own Mother Mary,

45:13.086 --> 45:14.337
and she... (INHALES)

45:14.879 --> 45:16.464
she was beautiful.

45:17.674 --> 45:19.217
But I'm the one
who had to go out

45:19.217 --> 45:20.844
in front of all those people

45:21.469 --> 45:23.263
and sing my songs

45:23.930 --> 45:26.182
and feel them, so, yes...

45:26.182 --> 45:27.225
(SCISSORS SNIP)

45:27.225 --> 45:29.853
...I wanted to change for her.

45:31.020 --> 45:32.897
But I was never done with us.

45:34.566 --> 45:35.984
You closed that door.

45:35.984 --> 45:38.862
No, there was never a door
at all until you opened it.

45:38.862 --> 45:39.946
The door doesn't exist.
(SCOFFS)

45:39.946 --> 45:41.948
These metaphors
are exhausting.

45:43.032 --> 45:44.117
(SCISSORS CLATTER)

45:45.243 --> 45:47.620
You went somewhere...

45:47.620 --> 45:50.206
-I couldn't follow.
-Yes, but you had all this.

45:50.206 --> 45:52.167
Yeah, I had to build this
so I had something.

45:52.167 --> 45:53.710
But that's good, isn't it?

45:53.710 --> 45:55.670
Yeah.

45:55.670 --> 45:58.381
Except that it took me
hating you to do it.

46:05.305 --> 46:07.140
-Uh-uh.
-(SCISSORS CLINKING)

46:08.057 --> 46:09.642
(SCISSORS SNIPPING)

46:11.436 --> 46:12.437
(WHIMPERS)

46:18.526 --> 46:19.527
(EXHALES)

46:22.906 --> 46:24.240
(SNIFFLES)

46:24.240 --> 46:25.783
You can't really hate me.

46:25.783 --> 46:26.868
Oh, yes, I can.

46:27.869 --> 46:30.538
It's very easy
to flip that switch.

46:30.538 --> 46:32.415
Is that what we're doing here?

46:32.415 --> 46:34.334
You're making me a hate-dress?

46:34.334 --> 46:35.710
Maybe.

46:36.503 --> 46:37.754
Maybe.

46:37.754 --> 46:40.048
So what do we have to do
to flip that switch back?

46:40.048 --> 46:42.717
I don't know. Maybe we can't,
maybe it's a one-time thing.

46:42.717 --> 46:43.718
No.

46:44.385 --> 46:45.887
You already have.

46:45.887 --> 46:47.847
You wouldn't let me
in the door otherwise.

46:47.847 --> 46:50.350
The real door
or the metaphorical one?

46:50.350 --> 46:51.851
-Your front door.
-Oh.

46:51.851 --> 46:53.978
Well... I didn't let you in.

46:55.146 --> 46:56.981
Hilda did.

46:56.981 --> 46:59.734
And why do I have to be
the one to open the door

46:59.734 --> 47:01.903
or flip a switch or whatever?

47:03.821 --> 47:05.198
Can't you do it?

47:07.283 --> 47:08.910
Can't you do the work?

47:10.870 --> 47:13.581
Make me love you again.

47:14.582 --> 47:16.292
Can you let me try?

47:17.669 --> 47:19.420
Can you stop putting up walls?

47:19.420 --> 47:22.090
Can you let me play
this fucking song?

47:22.090 --> 47:24.133
Oh, you can't do
anything else?

47:24.133 --> 47:25.969
I don't have anything else.

47:26.928 --> 47:28.304
What else is there?

47:28.304 --> 47:30.723
I can... send you flowers,

47:30.723 --> 47:32.684
I can write you a note,
or I can buy you a house,

47:32.684 --> 47:35.728
or I can sing you a song.
That's it.

47:37.063 --> 47:38.106
(CRIES SOFTLY)

47:40.692 --> 47:41.818
That's all I got.

47:45.238 --> 47:47.073
Well, I could do
with a new house.

47:47.073 --> 47:48.783
This one's falling apart.

47:50.618 --> 47:52.412
Pick one out
and send me the listing.

47:52.412 --> 47:54.205
Oh, you know, I think
I'll pay for it myself.

47:54.205 --> 47:56.207
Thank you very much.

47:56.207 --> 47:58.251
You see, the problem is,

47:58.251 --> 48:01.087
and it's not a problem,

48:01.087 --> 48:03.172
but the problem is...

48:04.007 --> 48:06.676
I am very stubborn.

48:07.302 --> 48:08.469
(SCOFFS)

48:09.470 --> 48:10.680
Clearly.

48:11.389 --> 48:13.808
And I don't...

48:13.808 --> 48:17.770
I'm no good
at changing on the spot.

48:18.938 --> 48:20.148
I'm not...

48:20.732 --> 48:22.233
like you.

48:23.484 --> 48:25.945
I can't be what other people
want me to be

48:25.945 --> 48:27.322
at the drop of a hat.

48:27.989 --> 48:29.282
Good.

48:30.074 --> 48:31.701
Because it wears you down.

48:31.701 --> 48:34.704
And I've been getting on
quite well without you.

48:34.704 --> 48:37.040
If I hear you on the radio,
I change the channel.

48:37.040 --> 48:39.459
If I see you on the telly,
I just turn it off.

48:41.044 --> 48:42.587
All or nothing.

48:44.505 --> 48:45.965
All or nothing.

48:48.426 --> 48:50.470
Everyone else needs you.

48:51.846 --> 48:53.389
I don't.

48:58.561 --> 49:00.521
Would you like to know
what happened

49:00.521 --> 49:02.690
the last time
I heard you sing?

49:03.900 --> 49:04.901
Sure.

49:04.901 --> 49:06.736
It's gonna sound
like another metaphor,

49:06.736 --> 49:08.196
even though it's not.

49:08.196 --> 49:09.197
Okay.

49:11.866 --> 49:15.662
Do you remember
when you played in Hyde Park

49:15.662 --> 49:17.747
at the beginning
of your Ecstatic Tour?

49:19.374 --> 49:21.376
-Yeah.
-I was there.

49:22.377 --> 49:23.628
Front row.

49:25.546 --> 49:27.298
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

49:35.306 --> 49:37.892
SAM: I wondered
if you'd spot me,

49:37.892 --> 49:40.228
but... you never did.

49:41.187 --> 49:43.773
Or if you did,
you didn't let on.

49:44.482 --> 49:46.484
And now I'm letting on now

49:47.860 --> 49:49.904
you were amazing.

49:50.988 --> 49:54.075
The whole crowd was crying.

49:54.575 --> 49:56.619
You were crying.

49:56.619 --> 49:58.121
And I was crying,

49:58.871 --> 50:01.791
but for a different reason.

50:01.791 --> 50:04.669
Because I was seeing
something beautiful

50:04.669 --> 50:06.462
that I had once been a part of

50:06.462 --> 50:09.298
and... never would be again.

50:11.050 --> 50:12.760
You were radiant.

50:14.512 --> 50:16.264
I was miserable.

50:16.889 --> 50:18.099
(SAM INHALES SLOWLY)

50:18.099 --> 50:19.267
And by and by,

50:19.267 --> 50:24.439
that misery resolved
into a very sharp pain

50:24.439 --> 50:26.441
in my upper mandible.

50:27.692 --> 50:30.820
My jaws were clenched so tight

50:30.820 --> 50:34.657
that my top left wisdom tooth
cracked wide open,

50:34.657 --> 50:37.744
and the pain that it gave me

50:37.744 --> 50:39.370
was pure

50:40.413 --> 50:41.664
and sharp.

50:43.166 --> 50:48.504
And I could think of no way
to describe it other than you.

50:48.504 --> 50:50.256
(INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

50:54.719 --> 50:56.053
Oh, it was you.

50:56.929 --> 50:59.140
And I had to cut you out.

51:02.769 --> 51:04.270
So I fled.

51:06.606 --> 51:08.858
Before the encore.

51:08.858 --> 51:10.234
Before you played Holy Spirit,

51:10.234 --> 51:12.904
the one song I thought
might make me feel better.

51:15.072 --> 51:16.407
AUDIENCE: Mary! Mary!

51:18.117 --> 51:19.410
(VOICE BREAKING) I ran home,

51:20.244 --> 51:21.621
grabbed some pliers,

51:23.748 --> 51:24.916
and...

51:27.835 --> 51:28.920
(TOOTH CRACKING)

51:31.172 --> 51:32.423
(MUSIC FADES)

51:35.259 --> 51:36.385
See?

51:39.680 --> 51:40.932
All gone.

51:42.767 --> 51:43.768
Jesus!

51:43.768 --> 51:45.978
(SNICKERING)
I'm only exaggerating.

51:47.063 --> 51:48.815
I went to the dentist.

51:49.816 --> 51:51.234
Yeah, they put me under,

51:52.485 --> 51:54.987
and when I woke up
in the chair,

51:55.571 --> 51:57.156
my tooth was gone.

51:59.325 --> 52:01.953
And the anesthesia
was wearing off,

52:03.704 --> 52:05.373
and I felt very sad.

52:06.916 --> 52:08.709
Like I was...

52:08.709 --> 52:12.255
in the midst of saying goodbye
to something dear.

52:12.964 --> 52:15.842
You know, when I was little,

52:15.842 --> 52:18.261
and we'd move,

52:18.261 --> 52:23.307
and I'd feel myself
being pulled away from a house

52:23.891 --> 52:26.519
I'd made time to love.

52:30.690 --> 52:31.691
Hmm.

52:34.277 --> 52:35.278
Now...

52:37.488 --> 52:38.990
this is where it gets

52:39.532 --> 52:40.533
strange.

52:41.909 --> 52:43.202
That night,

52:45.329 --> 52:46.581
I had a visitor.

52:48.207 --> 52:49.584
I woke up very suddenly

52:49.584 --> 52:51.669
to find that my gums
were bleeding again.

52:53.838 --> 52:56.382
There was blood all over.

52:56.382 --> 52:59.719
There was a little trail
of it, in fact,

52:59.719 --> 53:02.138
streaked across the duvet.

53:02.138 --> 53:05.349
It was like something had
crawled out of my mouth,

53:06.058 --> 53:07.768
across the bedspread,

53:08.686 --> 53:09.979
down onto the floor.

53:11.230 --> 53:12.356
Now...

53:13.190 --> 53:15.234
I've always been
open to ghosts.

53:15.234 --> 53:17.695
If any house was haunted,
you'd think it'd be this one,

53:17.695 --> 53:20.031
but I haven't seen one before.

53:20.907 --> 53:22.158
Until now.

53:22.909 --> 53:24.827
And I can say
without a doubt,

53:24.827 --> 53:27.830
there was a ghost
at the foot of my bed.

53:31.542 --> 53:33.044
What did it look like?

53:33.753 --> 53:35.880
I couldn't say.

53:35.880 --> 53:39.216
She was like
six different things at once.

53:39.592 --> 53:40.801
"She"?

53:40.801 --> 53:43.220
Yes. She was a she.

53:44.639 --> 53:46.432
I think.

53:46.432 --> 53:50.061
Or maybe the idea of a "she."

53:50.061 --> 53:51.604
(ETHEREAL MUSIC PLAYING)

53:51.604 --> 53:52.730
And she was red.

53:54.065 --> 53:56.067
Not red like a color.

53:56.734 --> 53:57.985
More like...

53:59.153 --> 54:01.030
red like a feeling.

54:01.030 --> 54:03.324
(WIND BLOWING)

54:09.705 --> 54:14.919
SAM: Oh, and she was
the most beautiful thing.

54:16.003 --> 54:18.172
I couldn't let her stay.

54:21.425 --> 54:23.636
So I opened the door,

54:24.887 --> 54:26.847
and I watched her go,

54:29.100 --> 54:30.518
down the hallway,

54:32.061 --> 54:33.854
out the house,

54:35.064 --> 54:37.483
into the woods,

54:37.483 --> 54:40.069
a smudge of red in the dark.

54:42.863 --> 54:46.617
Oh, and with her goes
the pain in my mouth,

54:48.536 --> 54:50.621
the knot in my stomach,

54:52.164 --> 54:54.625
and the hole in my heart.

54:58.295 --> 55:02.091
And after that I stopped
listening to your music.

55:04.051 --> 55:06.053
I stopped thinking about you.

55:07.179 --> 55:08.931
I stopped dreaming about you.

55:10.516 --> 55:14.270
And everything's been better
ever since.

55:17.481 --> 55:18.691
Where did she go?

55:19.859 --> 55:20.943
SAM: Oh.

55:22.069 --> 55:23.738
Oh, I don't know.

55:24.447 --> 55:25.614
Where do ghosts go

55:25.614 --> 55:27.324
when you don't
need 'em anymore?

55:28.159 --> 55:29.452
That's where.

55:29.452 --> 55:32.538
But are you saying that
this is just another metaphor?

55:32.538 --> 55:34.540
Did you really see something?

55:34.540 --> 55:37.418
Look, I'm not saying
that I saw the spirit

55:37.418 --> 55:39.628
of some
recently deceased individual

55:39.628 --> 55:44.050
or that my house
is haunted by an ancestor.

55:44.050 --> 55:45.342
If someone else...

55:45.342 --> 55:49.138
If Hilda, say, had been there,
would she have seen it?

55:49.138 --> 55:50.431
Probably not.

55:51.640 --> 55:52.808
But I did.

55:54.185 --> 55:56.437
Whatever neurons
in my head differentiate

55:56.437 --> 55:58.314
between imagination
and perception

55:58.314 --> 56:00.066
tell me that I did.

56:00.941 --> 56:04.111
And if you were
to ask me why I did,

56:05.071 --> 56:08.574
I would say
because I needed to.

56:09.450 --> 56:11.410
Perhaps I manifested her.

56:11.410 --> 56:15.122
Perhaps she was
my subconscious,

56:15.122 --> 56:16.165
sending me a message

56:16.165 --> 56:18.375
in the only way
it knew I would listen.

56:20.461 --> 56:22.379
Perhaps she was a ghost.

56:23.214 --> 56:24.256
Yeah.

56:27.510 --> 56:29.804
But she was my ghost.

56:31.597 --> 56:32.890
Except...

56:33.724 --> 56:35.601
I think I saw her too.

56:37.186 --> 56:38.604
You saw what?

56:38.604 --> 56:39.814
Your ghost.

56:39.814 --> 56:41.398
(UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING)

56:41.398 --> 56:43.442
-I saw her.
-I was being serious.

56:43.442 --> 56:44.819
So am I.

56:44.819 --> 56:47.113
So what?

56:47.113 --> 56:50.241
You can't even let me
have my own ghost story?

56:50.241 --> 56:52.201
No. No, it is yours.

56:52.201 --> 56:55.287
It is, but I think
I might be a part of it.

56:55.287 --> 56:57.498
You're making me feel

56:57.498 --> 56:59.875
-very foolish.
-I promise I don't mean to.

56:59.875 --> 57:02.169
(WHIMPERING)
I saw what you saw.

57:02.169 --> 57:07.925
I saw a ghost or a spirit
and she was red.

57:08.467 --> 57:10.594
And when was this?

57:10.594 --> 57:12.930
-The first time was...
-Ooh. "The first time"?

57:15.349 --> 57:17.226
The first time was in Dublin.

57:19.061 --> 57:20.688
96th stop of the tour.

57:21.480 --> 57:23.691
I was so worn out, but...

57:26.902 --> 57:28.487
it was my birthday.

57:31.073 --> 57:33.534
And I wanted to do
something special.

57:34.577 --> 57:36.036
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

57:36.036 --> 57:37.746
(CROWD CHEERING)

57:40.666 --> 57:42.751
I love you, Dublin!

57:42.751 --> 57:43.961
Goodnight!

57:43.961 --> 57:45.796
(CROWD CHEERING)

57:52.052 --> 57:54.096
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

58:05.941 --> 58:06.984
(MARY SIGHS)

58:07.484 --> 58:09.028
(MARY EXCLAIMS)

58:09.028 --> 58:11.238
-Thank you. (FLUTTERS LIPS)
-NIKKI: Here, here, here.

58:11.238 --> 58:12.781
I've got it. I've got it.
I've got it.

58:12.781 --> 58:14.074
MARY: (CHUCKLES) Careful.

58:14.074 --> 58:15.117
(MARY SIGHS)

58:16.452 --> 58:18.120
How does this keep happening?

58:19.580 --> 58:20.748
Oh, shit. Um,

58:20.748 --> 58:22.291
-there's blood on your...
-Huh?

58:22.291 --> 58:23.292
-JADE: Hey, MM!
-Blood...

58:23.292 --> 58:26.212
-Oh, um, yeah.
-JADE: Look who I found!

58:26.212 --> 58:27.254
MARY: Ooh.

58:27.796 --> 58:29.632
Oh, my gosh!

58:29.632 --> 58:30.799
-Are you...
-Hi.

58:30.799 --> 58:33.844
-(GIGGLING) Hi! Hi, hi, hi!
-I'm Imogen. Hi.

58:33.844 --> 58:35.596
-(MARY SIGHS)
-Happy birthday.

58:35.596 --> 58:37.306
Thank you. Thank you. Yes.

58:37.306 --> 58:38.891
-So nice to meet you.
-So nice to meet you.

58:38.891 --> 58:41.477
Yes. Oh, my gosh.
We are so excited for tonight.

58:41.477 --> 58:42.728
-Me too.
-Everyone says

58:42.728 --> 58:44.146
you are very special.

58:44.146 --> 58:46.065
-Well, that sounds very kind.
-Okay.

58:46.065 --> 58:47.483
JADE: She was sat
in the regular seat,

58:47.483 --> 58:48.734
that's why PJ couldn't
find her.

58:48.734 --> 58:49.985
-Ah.
-JADE: How long did you say

58:49.985 --> 58:51.528
-you waited in line?
-MARY: Oh?

58:51.528 --> 58:54.323
Only two hours.
But it's fine. I had fun.

58:54.323 --> 58:56.450
-I met people.
-I'm so sorry.

58:56.450 --> 58:57.910
Yeah. Okay.

58:57.910 --> 58:59.995
-I like meeting people.
-Thank you.

58:59.995 --> 59:02.456
Oh, well, now you're here
and you're with us.

59:02.456 --> 59:04.166
Did you like the show?

59:04.166 --> 59:05.960
-Oh, it was incredible.
-MARY: Mmm.

59:05.960 --> 59:08.379
It was like,
like a religious experience

59:08.379 --> 59:10.422
or like going to church,

59:10.422 --> 59:13.133
-but in a good way.
-(GIGGLING) Yeah.

59:13.133 --> 59:16.053
And at the same time,
all I could think is

59:16.053 --> 59:18.222
when you have
that many people...

59:18.222 --> 59:20.182
-Yeah.
-How many people were there?

59:20.182 --> 59:23.185
Uh, 18,210.

59:23.185 --> 59:25.312
There were even more
in New York.

59:25.312 --> 59:27.690
-(MARY EXCLAIMS)
-And they're all there,

59:27.690 --> 59:31.110
all at once,
putting out all that energy,

59:31.110 --> 59:33.070
all of those ups and downs,

59:33.070 --> 59:39.785
and all of it is
laser-focused right at you.

59:39.785 --> 59:42.246
Mmm. It's intense.

59:42.246 --> 59:43.622
How do you handle that?

59:44.498 --> 59:46.458
(SIGHS) You don't.

59:46.458 --> 59:48.502
Uh, I mean, you do.

59:48.502 --> 59:49.712
But you just...

59:49.712 --> 59:50.963
You sort of, um,

59:51.630 --> 59:52.631
take it

59:53.299 --> 59:54.383
and...

59:56.385 --> 59:57.928
(EXHALES SLOWLY)

01:00:00.931 --> 01:00:02.391
Yes, but...

01:00:03.642 --> 01:00:05.561
what does it do to you?

01:00:08.856 --> 01:00:10.941
It's like the same, same thing

01:00:10.941 --> 01:00:14.028
over and over again
in circles.

01:00:14.028 --> 01:00:15.237
GIRL: (GIGGLING)
Sounds like shit.

01:00:15.237 --> 01:00:17.281
IMOGEN: Don't ask
why he chose me, but he did.

01:00:17.281 --> 01:00:19.950
NIKKI: But you have seen
ghosts here before, right?

01:00:19.950 --> 01:00:21.368
IMOGEN: Ah, yes.

01:00:21.368 --> 01:00:23.078
There are spirits here

01:00:23.078 --> 01:00:24.872
and I've met most of them.

01:00:24.872 --> 01:00:27.583
But the walls here
are very thin.

01:00:27.583 --> 01:00:29.918
You never know
who might come knocking.

01:00:29.918 --> 01:00:32.963
Now, can somebody
get the lights?

01:00:32.963 --> 01:00:34.256
Do ghosts really need the dark

01:00:34.256 --> 01:00:36.592
or is it just
to make it spookier?

01:00:36.592 --> 01:00:38.385
IMOGEN: Oh, it's not for them.

01:00:38.385 --> 01:00:40.262
They're already here.

01:00:40.262 --> 01:00:42.598
We're the ones
that are opening up to them.

01:00:46.185 --> 01:00:47.478
(TINKLING)

01:00:51.065 --> 01:00:54.985
(CHANTING IN IRISH)

01:00:58.072 --> 01:00:59.239
(IN ENGLISH)
What does that mean?

01:00:59.239 --> 01:01:00.449
What does that mean?

01:01:00.449 --> 01:01:01.533
IMOGEN: It means

01:01:01.533 --> 01:01:03.660
-reveal yourselves.
-Reveal yourselves.

01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:05.662
- IMOGEN: We mean you no harm.
-We mean you no harm.

01:01:06.789 --> 01:01:08.499
Can I say it too?

01:01:08.499 --> 01:01:10.834
Yeah, sure.

01:01:10.834 --> 01:01:12.711
How does it go again?
(GIGGLES)

01:01:13.754 --> 01:01:15.297
(CHANTING IN IRISH)

01:01:15.297 --> 01:01:16.590
(CHANTING IN IRISH)

01:01:29.895 --> 01:01:33.857
(CHANTING IN IRISH)

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:47.037
(IMOGEN AND MARY
CONTINUE CHANTING)

01:01:55.129 --> 01:01:56.713
-(YELPS)
-(IN ENGLISH) No. No.

01:01:56.713 --> 01:01:58.048
Sorry, sorry. That was me.

01:01:58.048 --> 01:01:59.591
-Fuck you.
-Oh, my God.

01:01:59.591 --> 01:02:01.552
I slipped. I slipped.
I'm sorry.

01:02:01.552 --> 01:02:02.719
-I hate this.
-(GIRLS LAUGHING)

01:02:02.719 --> 01:02:05.013
I hate everything about this,
Emily. Really?

01:02:05.013 --> 01:02:06.765
-(GIRLS LAUGHING)
-Shh.

01:02:08.016 --> 01:02:09.643
(SHUSHING) Wait, wait, wait.

01:02:10.644 --> 01:02:11.687
What is it?

01:02:14.606 --> 01:02:15.732
Is someone here?

01:02:16.733 --> 01:02:18.152
Do you feel it?

01:02:18.152 --> 01:02:19.528
I feel nothing.

01:02:20.320 --> 01:02:21.822
What are we supposed to feel?

01:02:23.198 --> 01:02:26.910
She's not from here.

01:02:26.910 --> 01:02:27.911
"She"?

01:02:28.912 --> 01:02:31.790
She's from somewhere...

01:02:33.625 --> 01:02:35.002
far away.

01:02:39.798 --> 01:02:43.427
But she's very nearly here.

01:02:43.427 --> 01:02:45.304
Who are we talking about now?

01:02:46.597 --> 01:02:47.639
Who is she?

01:02:49.933 --> 01:02:50.976
Do you know?

01:02:52.728 --> 01:02:53.729
No.

01:02:58.692 --> 01:02:59.693
No.

01:03:05.782 --> 01:03:07.201
-No.
-(DISTORTED VOICE) No.

01:03:07.201 --> 01:03:08.535
Okay, we should...
Maybe this is just...

01:03:08.535 --> 01:03:10.829
-It's not real.
-She's just fucking with us.

01:03:10.829 --> 01:03:13.165
No, she isn't.

01:03:15.292 --> 01:03:17.169
(IN SING-SONG VOICE) Imogen...

01:03:18.921 --> 01:03:21.215
(SOFTLY) What do you want
to tell us?

01:03:21.215 --> 01:03:24.468
Do you have a message? Or...

01:03:25.469 --> 01:03:27.971
What do you want us to know?

01:03:30.474 --> 01:03:32.142
We're here for you.

01:03:38.315 --> 01:03:39.816
I'm here for you.

01:03:39.816 --> 01:03:41.151
(GASPS)

01:03:44.279 --> 01:03:46.448
I've been...

01:03:47.366 --> 01:03:48.492
looking...

01:03:49.493 --> 01:03:50.661
for you,

01:03:51.662 --> 01:03:54.831
my dearest one.

01:03:57.000 --> 01:04:01.171
I've come so far.

01:04:02.839 --> 01:04:03.882
(WHIMPERS SOFTLY)

01:04:04.550 --> 01:04:06.176
I've traveled

01:04:06.927 --> 01:04:11.890
across land and sea.

01:04:16.061 --> 01:04:17.354
(IMOGEN GRUNTS)

01:04:21.483 --> 01:04:22.693
-(TAPS FOOT)
-(BONES CRACK)

01:04:22.693 --> 01:04:24.736
-(THUNDER RUMBLES)
-(IMOGEN GASPS)

01:04:30.826 --> 01:04:33.954
-My feet are bleeding.
-MARY: ...bleeding.

01:04:37.207 --> 01:04:38.750
My bones...

01:04:39.418 --> 01:04:41.128
-MARY: Ache.
-...ache.

01:04:41.962 --> 01:04:43.338
My head...

01:04:43.338 --> 01:04:45.340
My head is heavy.

01:04:46.425 --> 01:04:48.427
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

01:04:51.430 --> 01:04:53.307
-See...
-MARY: See...

01:04:53.307 --> 01:04:54.725
in my hair...

01:04:56.476 --> 01:04:59.980
-a braid made of woe.
-MARY: A braid made of woe.

01:05:01.982 --> 01:05:04.860
See all your sorrows

01:05:06.153 --> 01:05:09.948
-hang over my shoulders.
-MARY: Hang over my shoulders.

01:05:09.948 --> 01:05:12.784
-And all of their kin...
-And all of their kin...

01:05:12.784 --> 01:05:16.288
-...bite at my heels.
-...bite at my heels.

01:05:16.288 --> 01:05:17.789
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)
-(GASPS)

01:05:26.715 --> 01:05:27.799
(WHIMPERING SOFTLY)

01:05:32.137 --> 01:05:33.138
(GRUNTS)

01:05:35.307 --> 01:05:37.476
IMOGEN: (INHALES SHARPLY)
But soon...

01:05:39.770 --> 01:05:43.357
